{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n**Inputs are presented through `NodeContents::format`.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` installs a custom formatter. It asserts that the user message sent to the agent contains \"formatted input: source\".\n- `fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` asserts that the node contents appear in the request, in order.\n- `fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` asserts the exact contents sent to the agent for queued inputs.\n\n**Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` mutates the underlying source after the read. It then asserts that `format()` still returns \"before\" and that `fingerprint()` equals the snapshot fingerprint.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` checks that formatting uses the supplied retained value and does not read the resource again.\n- The agent tests assert that the recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprint (\"source\") matches the content that was formatted. `fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` does this for two concurrent executions.\n\n**Loading or preparation failures on queued ask-builder inputs return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` covers a load failure (`fail_read`) and an edge-lookup failure (`fail_edges`). It also covers a preparation failure (`fail_prepare`).\n- Each case is asserted to return `Err(ValidationError::Graph(..))`. The test also asserts that no agent request is made and that no dependency is recorded.\n\n**Failures during a `read_node` tool call are returned to the agent as a tool error.**\n- `fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` has the formatter fail during `node_content`. It asserts that the second request's last message is a `ToolResult` with `is_error`, `name` \"read_node\" and the error text.\n- It also asserts that the agent then submits a result (the ask returns true), so the agent recovers. No dependency is recorded for the undelivered contents.\n- `read_node` in `tools.rs` and `Ask::execute` in `procedure.rs` both call `prepare_read` and propagate any error with `?`. A load failure takes the same mapping path as a preparation failure, so the missing load-failure variant for `read_node` is not a separate behavior that needs its own test.\n\nI found no obligation without a test, and no wrong expected result. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "8048d176a8293e95cc92aa446b4513cd36a149d6f42a172bff9e5eae9b604752",
